{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>And I will remember My covenant with Yaakov.</b> Because His bed was complete, no flaw is stated regarding him; and because all His years were in the covenant, He mentioned him first." "<b>And the land I will remember.</b> Because it was stated above: 'And I will lay the land most desolate,' and 'your land shall not give its yield.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The wordplay involves יעקב/יעקוב and מטה/מטתו (bed/staff), echoing the well-known rabbinic dictum about Jacob's bed being שלמה (complete)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:42.682298185Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}